L000521	\subsection{Scaling of the inverse gap}
L000522	The scaling of the disorder-averaged fundamental gap $[\Delta]$ (we identified $\Delta \equiv \Delta_o$) for the quantum SK model is analyzed in the main text. Hereafter, we consider instead the scaling of the disorder average $[\eta]$ of the inverse gap $\eta=1/\Delta$. As shown in Fig.~\ref{figSM4}, the scaling with system size $N$ is well approximated by a power-law function $[\eta]\propto N^{0.33}$.
L000523	Notice that this exponent turns out to agree with the scaling of the inverse of the disorder-averaged gap.
